# "You" in Wedding Announcement's trigger is whoever controls it, and a copy is controlled by the player who copies it
# (CR 707.10). Bot1 attacks with two Ornithopters on turn 3, so its own trigger draws. In that end step Bot2 copies the
# trigger with Return the Favor: Bot2 declared no attackers (only the active player does, CR 506.2, 508.1a), so the copy
# gives Bot2 a Human and no card, and puts a second counter on the enchantment, the same source (CR 707.10b).
[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Wedding Announcement
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Return the Favor
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wedding Announcement.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Return the Favor.Cast
Bot2.Modes(Copy target)
Bot2.Target(Stack.Wedding Announcement)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Wedding Announcement.Counters.Invitation = 2
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
